  "after_visit_summary": "You have coronary artery disease with a stent that is stable. Your LDL cholesterol is high at 118, and we need it under 55 to protect your heart. You had muscle aches in your legs from atorvastatin 80 mg, so we are switching your cholesterol medicine. Start rosuvastatin 5 mg by mouth once daily and ezetimibe 10 mg by mouth once daily. If muscle aches return, stop the rosuvastatin and message us, but keep taking the ezetimibe. Continue taking aspirin 81 mg once daily, clopidogrel 75 mg once daily until February, and metoprolol 25 mg once daily. Do not stop clopidogrel without talking to us first. Keep walking 30 minutes most days. We will recheck your cholesterol and liver tests in 8 weeks. If your LDL is still above 55, we may discuss injectable cholesterol medicines. Follow up with us in 3 months. Watch for unexplained muscle pain, weakness, or dark urine, and contact us if these occur.",
